Production employee
Day Shift / 21-40 hours per week / Utrecht
🌟 In short

  - Fixed day shift hours (07:00-16:30)

  - Choose your workweek: 3, 4, or 5 fixed weekdays

  - Clean working environment

💼 The position

As a production employee, you ensure that hotels and restaurants are supplied daily with fresh, clean linen. This includes items such as napkins, tablecloths, towels, pillowcases, and duvet covers. Using modern machines, the linen is washed, ironed, and folded. You will be actively working and moving throughout the day 💪.

Together with your colleagues, you make sure everything runs smoothly. Your main tasks include:

  - Sorting the linen;

  - Loading the linen into the machines piece by piece;

  - Checking the quality;

  - Placing stacks of linen neatly into the roll containers.

💰 What we offer

  - Starting salary of € 15.33 gross per hour (€ 14.99 + € 0.34 allowance);

  - After 6 months: € 15.45 gross per hour + € 0.82 year-end allowance (5.33%);;

  - Flexible workweek: choose 3, 4, or 5 fixed weekdays;

  - A Stable job with fixed working hours;

  - 25 vacation days, 8.33% holiday pay, and travel allowance (5–40 km one way);

  - Career growth opportunities, e.g., to shift supervisor or operator.

👀 What we expect from you

  - You speak Dutch or English;

  - You live in the Utrecht area (within 25 km of our laundry);

  - You are available for at least 3 fixed weekdays (07:00 – 16:30);

  - You are proactive and enjoy staying active;

  - You have a flexible work attitude.

📞 Interested?

For more information or to apply, contact Hester Visser (HR):

📞 Call: 030 307 2200

 💬 WhatsApp: 06 2539 7485

 📧 Email: werkenbij@vanderkleijtextiel.nl

Or view the vacancy online on our website:

https://werkenbij.vanderkleijtextiel.nl/en/production-personnel/

    Interesse in de functie van Production employee bij Wasserij & Linnenverhuur G. van der Kleij & Zn. bv regio Utrecht?

Reageer nu met je CV en motivatie v

- Venlo - 40 uur - € 17,47 per uur 
Are you looking for a challenging position as a Reachstacker Driver in Venlo? Do you enjoy working with heavy equipment and keeping a cool head in a dynamic terminal environment? At the terminal in Greenport Venlo, containers from sea, road, and rail come together. You ensure that everything is handled safely, efficiently, and on time. No container is too heavy, and no schedule is too tight. Thanks to your experience and expertise, the terminal keeps moving day and night 
What do we offer? 
• An hourly wage of €17,47, including shift allowances; 
• Working in a 2-shift system between 06:00 and 00:00; 
• Working one Saturday every four weeks, compensated as time off in lieu; 
• A solid pension scheme; 
• Full travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometre; 
• The opportunity to work with modern and well-maintained equipment; 
• Career development opportunities within a growing family-owned company; 
• A varied position in a professional terminal environment. 
What will you do? - Load and unload containers from trucks and rail wagons; - Move and correctly position containers in the stack using the reachstacker; - Occasionally operate the terminal tractor to move trailers; - Coordinate with planning, gate operations, and colleagues on the terminal; - Monitor safety, quality, and efficiency at all times; - Respond quickly to changes in the planning; - Work in a 2-shift schedule. 
What do you bring? - Experience as a Reachstacker Driver is a strong advantage; - No reachstacker experience yet, but affinity with logistics and experience operating a forklift or reach truck? We also encourage you to apply; - You take responsibility for your work and your machine; - You remain calm and flexible when situations change; - You have a good command of Dutch or, at the very least, good English communication skills; - You are willing to work in shifts; - Safety is always your top priority. 
Interested in applying? Please ...

Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!
